  "words": "A folded card spacer can be designed from the card thickness and a crease allowance measured once for each stock. For heights up to 2 mm the thin and medium stocks follow the layer model closely, and they are the better choice when a rail must sit at an exact height. The thick stock is quicker to fold but should be checked in the slot when more than three layers are used. A card ladder (Window Frame Study, 2021) gives a convenient way to check many spacers at once.",
